Z||000000||BroCar 87||11-24-2000||12:27 AM||||Hey guys, I have a couple questions on raising a fiero like a 4X4. I have seen this done on a couple of fieros, and wouldn't mind playing around in the mud with my toy fiero. REMEMBER this is not my daily driver fiero, this is my PARTS/TOY fiero. Its an 84 SE. <BR>Does anyone know how to go about doing this?<BR>I am just thinking of this idea right now, its not a SET idea. <BR>Any info on this would be greatly appreciated.<BR>Thanks for the space. (hoping for a reply)<BR>BroCar 87<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature2.jpg">  <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>   Custom dual side exit exhaust!||||reg||6
Z||000001||kinboyatuwo||11-24-2000||09:27 AM||||I have seen some pics on a fiero web site, can't remember where though, good luck<P>it did look cool though!||||reg||4
Z||000002||rockcrawl||11-24-2000||09:32 AM||||I've seen Subaru lift kits that use a spacer between the top of the strut and the frame. That would work on the rear of a Fiero, but not the front. I suppose the entire front crossmember could be lowered down from the frame. Why not just cut out the fenders and bolt on some 30" tires. The tires alone would give you a lot more ground clearance.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||onfire||11-24-2000||09:38 AM||||Ask these guys. <A HREF="http://www.cybercars.com/mnfr/fierohq/jalapeno.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cybercars.com/mnfr/fierohq/jalapeno.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>"I seen it on the internet, and I believe everthing on the net."<BR><A HREF="http://homestead.deja.com/user.on_fire/on_fire.html" TARGET=_blank>Check out my waist of banbwidth.</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||2xsess||11-24-2000||12:09 PM||||Bob Parker at Kickhill used a 4x4 Chevy Luv chassis for his 4x4 Fiero. I know there's pics here somewhere on the forum, just look for posts about the show at his place.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||BroCar 87||11-24-2000||04:44 PM||||Thanks guys!!<BR>on fire: I gave them an email. It shows that they used a "RYANE MOTORSPORTS" suspension kit, which raised the fiero 3 inches. I believe that is what I am looking for. <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature2.jpg">  <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>   Custom dual side exit exhaust!||||reg||6
